{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-128784","model_call":42,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1344"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1344"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_1263459082#0_2574610828","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1344","rank":2,"snippet":"that millions of people will use for years. Whether your career goals are professional satisfaction or financial success, education and planning can assist you in meeting those goals. Education Requirements The minimum education requirement for civil engineering occupations is a bachelor’s degree. Employers prefer candidates who attend an educational program approved by the Accreditation Board for Engineering and Technology. Obtaining a bachelor’s degree from an accredited educational program is required to be licensed as a professional engineer. Accredited educational programs typically include work experience as an intern to prepare you for a <cover>civil engineering career. Engineering Licensure Civil engineers often work on infrastructure </cover>projects that provide services to the public, which requires a professional engineer license in most states. Two exams are required to obtain a license. The aim of an aspiring civil engineer is to sit for and pass the Fundamentals of Engineering exam administered by the National Council of Examiners for Engineering and Surveying during your senior year of undergraduate studies.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"Civil Engineering Career Goals | Work - Chron.com\" , \"url\": \"https://work.chron.com/"},"time":2},"model_calls":42,"document_judgments":41,"relevance_3":31,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
